    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2022-tame-07: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.03";
    dc:description "The text presents these three capacities as the basic hallmarks TAME will use. A system that shows them fits the definition, and a system that lacks them falls outside it. Public data can hunt for the capacities and cannot confirm or refute the stipulation that they are what a Self is.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Goals, associative memory, and credit assignment can be measured in a particular system, but finding them would illustrate this definition of a Self rather than test it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "The statement stipulates the hallmarks of a Self, so empirical cases are examples of the definition.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.88"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.03"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
